87318a2fb7fffeb72adca934e31915be077c3d1f\r\n\r\n### System information\r\n\r\nWindows 11 Pro\r\n\r\n### Issue description\r\n\r\nWhen using the godot editor to export a PCK file using --export-pack command and using the exact same export preset, same encryption key, and exact same file inputs, without any single change on anything on the disk, each time the PCK is generated it may have different binary data, even though it will have exact same byte size on disk and of file, when you generate hashes from the file content (like for checking if there was a change on the PCK file between versions), it generates a different hash (while it should be generating the exact same hash), which means that building an PCK of the exact same data with exact same everything, outputs a different PCK binary for some reason (may be cause it is saving the data on the PCK in different order each time perhaps?). This makes extremely hard to make complex update systems that detects changes on the PCK data files based on their hash, as even if no data got changed, the PCK will have a different hash than other PCK generated in another run.\r\nHere a quick sample using SHA-512, both files were generated 1 after the other, by running the same command on same data:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/efcb7b85-091b-4036-81ad-4c7d3e6f4b69)\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3c9acccd-6dbe-4f37-863d-37df415812b0)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nSimple use --export-pack to export a PCK containing some files (I've tried with textures for example, and used the same encryption key on all the tests) and every time you pack the exact same files on exact same manner, it outputs an PCK with different binary content (generating a different hash).\r\n\r\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\r\n\r\nThis happens when running the --export-pack command from the editor to pack files.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky